{"4972400": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Refund Speedrun", "steam_appid": 4972400, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/3f3e680499ddc49571735e69f18774ef.avif?t=1788255640\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras_big/3f3e680499ddc49571735e69f18774ef.webp?t=1788255640 width=1560 height=163 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're a support agent at DrumWorks (any resemblance to existing platforms is</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >purely coincidental) with exactly one job: approve or deny refund requests for</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >video games. Read the complaint, check it against the policy, click APPROVE or</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >DENY — and pray you hit quota before your manager notices you haven't.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The apartment</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/8d0724f531d1835290b005d955904780.poster.avif?t=1788255640\" width=720 height=406 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/8d0724f531d1835290b005d955904780.webm?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/8d0724f531d1835290b005d955904780.mp4?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After hours you crawl back to the dump grandma left you (rest her soul). Manage</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >a deeply sophisticated needs system: bowel, shower, kebab intake. Pay the water</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >bill. Buy furniture, paint the walls, unlock rooms, exterminate cockroaches.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And look after grandma's fish — or flush them, they don't mind.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Coffee buys you a few more hours. Just… go easy on the coffee.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The job</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/40070062e700aabb9fae2913fe5d23d1.webp?t=1788255640\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/40070062e700aabb9fae2913fe5d23d1.poster.avif?t=1788255640\" class=\"bb_img\" width=720 height=406 /></picture></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every case is a little puzzle. One guy wants a refund after 40 hours played.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The next one is actually right. All you have is a 16-rule policy and a hunch.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Get it right and you climb five support tiers. Get it wrong and Jarek, your</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >manager, will remind you. By email. Then another. Then a third.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >...and then</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/e25769b5e9699a6508ecc90ffccdea40.poster.avif?t=1788255640\" width=720 height=406 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/e25769b5e9699a6508ecc90ffccdea40.webm?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/e25769b5e9699a6508ecc90ffccdea40.mp4?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The terminal starts acting up.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cases arrive that can't be handled the normal way — complaints from accounts</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >that were never created, playtime that runs backwards, a refund request for a</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >game nobody has ever shipped. The screen shows you things it shouldn't. The</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >apartment does not stay the way you left it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turns out grandma left you more than an aquarium and some damp. And somebody</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >really does not want you digging into it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What you actually do</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rule the queue by a 16-rule refund policy — every case is decidable, and</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >every wrong call is on you</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Climb five support tiers under a quota that does not care about your night</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Run a filthy inherited apartment: needs, bills, furniture, paint, roaches</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Keep the fish alive. Or don't.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Follow grandma's questline into the part of this job nobody documented</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The policy has 16 rules. None of them cover this.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/3f3e680499ddc49571735e69f18774ef.avif?t=1788255640\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras_big/3f3e680499ddc49571735e69f18774ef.webp?t=1788255640 width=1560 height=163 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're a support agent at DrumWorks (any resemblance to existing platforms is</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >purely coincidental) with exactly one job: approve or deny refund requests for</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >video games. Read the complaint, check it against the policy, click APPROVE or</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >DENY — and pray you hit quota before your manager notices you haven't.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The apartment</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/8d0724f531d1835290b005d955904780.poster.avif?t=1788255640\" width=720 height=406 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/8d0724f531d1835290b005d955904780.webm?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/8d0724f531d1835290b005d955904780.mp4?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After hours you crawl back to the dump grandma left you (rest her soul). Manage</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >a deeply sophisticated needs system: bowel, shower, kebab intake. Pay the water</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >bill. Buy furniture, paint the walls, unlock rooms, exterminate cockroaches.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And look after grandma's fish — or flush them, they don't mind.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Coffee buys you a few more hours. Just… go easy on the coffee.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The job</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/40070062e700aabb9fae2913fe5d23d1.webp?t=1788255640\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/40070062e700aabb9fae2913fe5d23d1.poster.avif?t=1788255640\" class=\"bb_img\" width=720 height=406 /></picture></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every case is a little puzzle. One guy wants a refund after 40 hours played.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The next one is actually right. All you have is a 16-rule policy and a hunch.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Get it right and you climb five support tiers. Get it wrong and Jarek, your</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >manager, will remind you. By email. Then another. Then a third.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >...and then</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/e25769b5e9699a6508ecc90ffccdea40.poster.avif?t=1788255640\" width=720 height=406 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/e25769b5e9699a6508ecc90ffccdea40.webm?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/extras/e25769b5e9699a6508ecc90ffccdea40.mp4?t=1788255640\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The terminal starts acting up.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cases arrive that can't be handled the normal way — complaints from accounts</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >that were never created, playtime that runs backwards, a refund request for a</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >game nobody has ever shipped. The screen shows you things it shouldn't. The</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >apartment does not stay the way you left it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turns out grandma left you more than an aquarium and some damp. And somebody</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >really does not want you digging into it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >What you actually do</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rule the queue by a 16-rule refund policy — every case is decidable, and</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >every wrong call is on you</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Climb five support tiers under a quota that does not care about your night</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Run a filthy inherited apartment: needs, bills, furniture, paint, roaches</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Keep the fish alive. Or don't.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Follow grandma's questline into the part of this job nobody documented</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The policy has 16 rules. None of them cover this.</p>", "short_description": "You're a support agent at DrumWorks, approving or denying game refund requests by a 16-rule policy. Hit quota. Pay the water bill. Feed grandma's fish. Then the terminal starts showing you things it shouldn't — and you find out what else she left you.", "supported_languages": "English, Polish", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/4a0540d3edc367791ff66a4de907b9b641b3c3d4/header.jpg?t=1788255640", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/0b23f38880005bf05a5531b059fef5bff1cdea72/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1788255640", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4972400/0b23f38880005bf05a5531b059fef5bff1cdea72/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1788255640", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i3-4130 (3.4GHz) / AMD FX-6300<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong>  Intel HD Graphics 4400 / NVIDIA GeForce GT 730 (1GB VRAM, OpenGL 3.3)<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 700 MB avail